    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Postfix / Mailman delivery signals",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus-mail"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### signal not exported yet\n\nThe panels this row would hold cannot be built today. The cluster Prometheus (`prometheus-mail`) scrapes only these jobs: `kepler`, `kube-state-metrics`, `node-bumble`, `node-honey`, `node-relay`, `node-sting`, `nut-exporter`, `prometheus`, `rspamd`. No metric name below exists in any datasource on this Grafana; none has been invented here.\n\n| Wanted signal | Metric that would carry it | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Postfix queue depth (active/deferred/hold) | `postfix_showq_message_size_bytes` / `postfix_queue_length` (postfix_exporter) | **absent** \u2014 no postfix_exporter runs |\n| Delivery rate | `postfix_smtp_delivery_*` | **absent** |\n| Deferral / bounce rate | `postfix_smtpd_messages_*`, bounce counters | **absent** |\n| Mailman list traffic (posts, held, rejected) | `mailman_*` (no upstream exporter is deployed) | **absent** |\n| Subscriber count for keyholders@ | Mailman REST API scrape | **absent** |\n| Dovecot / IMAP sessions | `dovecot_*` | **absent** |\n\n**About rspamd**: this Prometheus *does* carry `rspamd_scanned_total`, `rspamd_actions_total`, `rspamd_spam_total` and `rspamd_ham_total` \u2014 but every series is labelled `namespace=\"tinyland-dev-production\"`, pod `rspamd-normal-*`. That is the Tinyland substrate's scanner, **not** a GFTB tenant signal, so it is deliberately not charted on a GFTB dashboard. Charting it here would attribute another tenant's mail volume to GFTB.\n\n**Loki is not an option today either**: the Loki datasource (uid `loki`) holds logs for exactly one namespace, `tinyland-staging`. There are zero log streams for `latoolb-us-production`, so no log-derived queue/delivery panel can be built. Lighting these up needs an Alloy/Promtail scrape covering the GFTB namespaces, plus a postfix/Mailman exporter beside the list engine \u2014 both operator-gated changes outside this ticket."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Contact-form endpoint and Anubis challenge signals",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus-mail"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 29
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### signal not exported yet\n\nThe panels this row would hold cannot be built today. The cluster Prometheus (`prometheus-mail`) scrapes only these jobs: `kepler`, `kube-state-metrics`, `node-bumble`, `node-honey`, `node-relay`, `node-sting`, `nut-exporter`, `prometheus`, `rspamd`. No metric name below exists in any datasource on this Grafana; none has been invented here.\n\n| Wanted signal | Metric that would carry it | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Contact-form submit rate | form-handler `/metrics` | **absent** \u2014 the form-handler pod exposes no metrics endpoint to this Prometheus |\n| Form 4xx / 5xx rate | form-handler `/metrics` or ingress metrics | **absent** |\n| Anubis challenge issued / passed / failed | `anubis_challenges_*` | **absent** \u2014 both `anubis` and `anubis-archive` run, neither is scraped |\n| ALTCHA proof-of-work verification failures | form-handler `/metrics` | **absent** |\n| Rate-limit / abuse rejections | form-handler or edge logs | **absent** |\n\nWhat *is* visible for these components on this dashboard is workload state only: the `form-handler`, `anubis` and `anubis-archive` Deployments appear in the replica, restart, waiting-reason and image-digest panels above. That answers \"is the form path up?\" but not \"is the form path being used, and is it rejecting anything?\".\n\nPrivacy constraint on any future implementation: `meta/spec/observability-shape-2026-06-05.md` forbids PII and client IPs in the telemetry pipeline. Form panels must count events by outcome only \u2014 never by submitter, address, or IP."
      }
    }
